WEBVTT

00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:17,140
I reached five years and my oncologist took me off the horrible blocker at Astrosol.

00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:23,140
I have been off it for about a week, should I get retested?

00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:29,140
And I think the person saying, should I get to do another cheek swab test?

00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:33,140
Maybe not.

00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:43,140
So if you're on a horrible blocky therapy, so if you have a positive ER positive or hurtful positive cancer,

00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:51,140
typically, they're going to put you on an enromatase inhibitor that's going to block all your hormones.

00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:56,140
If you reach a certain point, I mean, I'm surprised that they're taking you off after five years,

00:00:56,140 --> 00:01:00,140
and the oncologist will keep people on for ten years now.

00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:04,140
It used to be much shorter than five years that they would keep you on.

00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:10,140
But now, I guess the rule of thumb, at least for that oncologist's office, is to take you off if you've got a clean meal of health.

00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:13,140
That five years, first of all, congratulations for that.

00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:18,140
Give God the praise for healing you and keeping you in a healed state.

00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:24,140
Now we want to keep you in that healed state as much as possible doing our part, right?

00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:30,140
If you have a horrible positive cancer and they take you off of the horrible blocker,

00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:37,140
I would definitely go on a natural aerobotase inhibitor for sure.

00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:40,140
Do we need to do a cheek swab test for that?

00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:43,140
Not necessarily.

00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:47,140
Honestly, I would just go on a roba clear.

00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:54,140
That's our most balanced or natural aerobotase inhibitor, and I would take three of those a day, a roba clear.

00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:57,140
That's our private label product, and I would take three of those a day.

00:01:57,140 --> 00:02:00,140
I don't think you need to do another cheek swab test.

00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:04,140
Now, if you haven't done a cheek swab test forever and ever, then that's another thing.

00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:07,140
But if you've done a cheek swab test in the last six months,

00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:10,140
and the only change that you're making is going off and asking,

00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:15,140
I would just go on a roba clear three per day and call it good,

00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:21,140
and we could do it on a cheek swab test after three or four months and see if anything's changed

00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:25,140
to be able to offer that medication.

